<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suwałki</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suwałki is a town in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, in Podlaskie Voivodeship near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. It lies in the former land of the Sudovians and grew from a settlement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camaldolese">Camaldolese</a> monks of Wigry in the early 18th century. It gives its name to the Suwałki Gap, the stretch of the Polish–Lithuanian border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> and Russia's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Kaliningrad</a> region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suwalki.jpg" alt="Suwałki" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sławomir Milejski · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SM_Suwa%C5%82ki_Ko%C5%9Bci%C3%B3%C5%82_%C5%9Bw_Aleksandra_2020_(2)_(cropped)2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
